OneiOS take18, userland/metal/patches/metal2vulkan/0007: at a memory pressure rise the parked images and buffers go
first, so the blocks they lie in are freed with the kept ones.
Upstream: Droid-VM/NativeMetal 4411df9 (UniXNU line, 2026-11-11), bridge/patches/0034-parked-objects-and-kept-blocks-
age-by-time.patch: its recycle.rs, buffer.rs and texture.rs hunks verbatim (Recycler::aged, Device::age_parked_images,
Device::age_parked_buffers; one doc comment names our callers) and its release_kept_memory hunk. Not taken: its room
thread's timed pass and age_kept (they sit on UniXNU's 0027/0030, which our room.rs has not), Device::age_parked and
spare_age. The aging by time at idle is metal2vulkan 0006's (upstream OneiOS cb32176: the 2 s idle trim frees the
objects parked past their second); this patch adds what 0006 leaves out, the memory pressure path.
What: Device::release_kept_memory, inside its exit-guard section, lets every parked image and buffer go before it frees
the spare and kept empty blocks. The frontend's pressure handler (NativeBridgeMetalFrontend.mm watchImportPressure, at a
warning or critical level) calls nmb_device_trim_memory(0) and then nmb_device_release_kept_memory, so the blocks the
parked objects emptied go in that same call (release_spare frees every spare and kept empty block).
Why: a parked object keeps its placement, so its block stays live. Before, the pressure path freed only blocks with
nothing placed in them: the up to 32 images / 128 MiB and 64 buffers / 64 MiB a process keeps parked (recycle.rs
bounds) held their blocks through the pressure rise, every block wired guest memory.
Risk: low. A making after the rise builds its VkImage or VkBuffer again (as for an object a take found stale); each
release runs through release.rs, in a section of the exit guard.
Switch: none (pressure only). Removable: yes (ONEIOS_METAL_SKIP=parked-objects-go-at-memory-pressure); applies with or
without 0006.

